  concept: "Authored objective: Repair R7, V05 and Q1 with fresh retests.\nAuthored
    requirement: Recorded from the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and
    the level\u2019s verified run history.\nGeneral teaching principle: Troubleshooting
    compares fresh evidence with a known reference, isolates likely causes, repairs
    the supported issue and retests.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can
    establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: Debugging a chain is easier when each link is tested before replacing
    the next.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An absent output is a symptom, not definitive proof that one specific
    component has failed.
